{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1503514-fire-dragon-style-rewrite","id":1503514,"title":"Fire Dragon Style (Rewrite)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-20T01:25:05-08:00","id":1503514,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Fire Dragon Style (Rewrite)","content":"I was looking over Short Sword style in Exalted before my mind wandered to Fire Dragon. Fire Dragon has many of the problems I felt with Solars: Dice tricks and lack of really cool charms. This isn\u2019t unique to Ex3, it\u2019s a problem that has existed even in Ex2 where this style\u2019s main claim to fame was the insane amount of attacks you could do with flurries. When browsing through the homebrew folder of Ex2 stylists, I came across JiveX\u2019s old rewrite of Fire Dragon, which attempted to fix the issues of the style. After reading it, I felt inspired as I did when I first read it, the only difference being that I can actually write mechanics which I feel do the style justice. It also helps I can get rid of the stupid aura mechanic and allow non-DB\u2019s to also join in on this style\u2019s fun.<br /> <br /> The focus of this style is a fast and hard offensive style. Your character strikes hard, fast, and constantly keeps pressure on the opponent. The more pressure you put on them the stronger your charms become. Even if your attack doesn't defeat your opponent, you can easily leave a lasting impression that they won't easily be rid of.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hV89ZYG1xcXhAL7y02MhSeTLB56o0vbhcVB78P90taU/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Now burn them. </a><i><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hV89ZYG1xcXhAL7y02MhSeTLB56o0vbhcVB78P90taU/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Burn them all</a>.\u200b</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/>